## Context

The post-review full gate for ticket 0829 exposed six failures that reproduce
unchanged on `main` at `51c451d4`.  Five failures compare the current
authoritative JETP observatory views (overview, ZAF, IDN, VNM, SEN) with the
frozen `mvp-baseline-0761.zip`; the current source cutoff/content has moved
beyond that baseline.  The sixth rebuilds the ZAF migration and obtains 1,087
legacy dispositions while the test expects 1,084.

This is a science-lane consistency defect between live JETP data, frozen
publication artifacts, and acceptance assertions.  It is not caused by the
0829 module extraction: the exact failures were reproduced in the unmodified
primary checkout, while the 0822 snapshot tests and byte replay remain green.

## First test (Red)

Run:

`uv run --env-file .env python -m pytest tests/test_jetp_compatibility.py tests/test_jetp_zaf_migration.py::test_zaf_candidate_reconciles_inventory_legacy_and_unchanged_views -q`

The expected current result is `6 failed, 5 passed`: overview plus four country
views diverge from the 0761 baseline, and the ZAF migration reports 1,087
legacy dispositions instead of 1,084.

## Investigation boundary

Determine whether the current authoritative inputs are an intended new
publication edition or accidental drift.  Do not update a baseline or relax a
count until the source revisions, cutoff, and three additional ZAF dispositions
have been identified and adjudicated.  Regenerate artifacts from their source;
never hand-edit generated JSON/ZIP content.

## Exit criteria

- [x] The three extra ZAF legacy dispositions are identified by stable IDs and
      classified as intended additions or corrected upstream drift.
- [x] The observatory cutoff/source changes behind each of the five MVP view
      mismatches are documented and adjudicated.
- [x] Current builders and checked-in preview views agree exactly; the distinct
      immutable 0761 baseline remains pinned independently by the byte size and
      SHA-256 in `docs/jetp-mvp-baseline-0761.json`.
- [x] The targeted suite passes while retaining both guards and explicit ZAF
      per-table counts.
- [x] `make check-fast`, `make lint`, and `make check` pass, or any remaining
      pre-existing full-gate failure is independently reproduced and ticketed.
